Article 4 Where the rural land contract arbitration committee submits a party's application for property preservation to the People's Court according to law, the party applying for property preservation shall be the applicant.

The rural land contract arbitration committee shall submit the following materials:

(1) a written application for property preservation;

(2) the notice of case acceptance issued by the rural land contract arbitration committee;

(3) proof of the applicant's identity;

(4) specific information on the property for which preservation is sought.

Where the People's Court adopts preservation measures, it may order the applicant to provide a guarantee; if the applicant does not provide a guarantee, it shall rule to reject the application.

Article 8 Where the rural land contract arbitration committee submits a party's application for evidence preservation to the People's Court according to law, it shall provide the following materials:

(1) a written application for evidence preservation;

(2) the notice of case acceptance issued by the rural land contract arbitration committee;

(3) proof of the applicant's identity;

(4) specific information on the evidence for which preservation is sought.

For specific procedural matters of evidence preservation, the provisions of Articles 5, 6, and 7 of this Interpretation concerning property preservation shall apply.

Article 9 After the rural land contract arbitration committee makes an advance ruling, where a party applies according to law to the Primary People's Court at the domicile of the person subject to enforcement or at the place where the property subject to enforcement is located for enforcement, the People's Court shall accept and enforce it.

To apply for enforcement of an advance ruling, the following materials shall be provided:

(1) a written application for enforcement;

(2) the advance ruling made by the rural land contract arbitration committee;

(3) proof of the identity of the applicant for enforcement;

(4) the guarantee provided by the applicant for enforcement;

(5) other documents or certificates that shall be submitted.
